      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Implementation**\n\nI'm solidifying the implementation plan. My current focus is choosing a concrete external provider for metric retrieval. I've decided on Google Cloud Monitoring. Now I'm preparing to specify how to integrate the API into a `aggregate_metric_stats.py` Python file.\n\n\n**Refining the Approach**\n\nI'm now fully committed to Google Cloud Monitoring. I've broken down the implementation steps. The goal is a Python script, `aggregate_metric_stats.py`, to get time-windowed metric data. My next step is fleshing out the code, with specific library imports, client creation, and function definitions. The function will accept project ID, metric type, and a time window. It will use `list_time_series` to query, with specified aggregation.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789863506081,
          "start": 1789863502742
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc2da396001G0bt06Fw6FtuaO",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc2d9e230014F3V3UO899KTw2",
      "session_id": "ses_f43d261eeffeYA7D1EtH1BGCU9",
      "time_created": 1789863502742,
      "time_updated": 1789863506081
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "t2FbuvhfUO12UG6k",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import monitoring_v3\nfrom google.protobuf import timestamp_pb2\nimport datetime\n\ndef aggregate_metric_stats(project_id: str, metric_type: str, minutes: int):\n    \"\"\"Retrieves aggregated statistics for a metric over a time window.\n\n    Args:\n        project_id: Your Google Cloud project ID.\n        metric_type: The type of the metric (e.g., \"compute.googleapis.com/instance/cpu/utilization\").\n        minutes: The number of minutes for the aggregation window.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = monitoring_v3.MetricServiceClient()\n    project_name = f\"projects/{project_id}\"\n\n    now = datetime.datetime.now(tz=datetime.timezone.utc)\n    end_time = timestamp_pb2.Timestamp()\n    end_time.FromDatetime(now)\n    start_time = timestamp_pb2.Timestamp()\n    start_time.FromDatetime(now - datetime.timedelta(minutes=minutes))\n\n    interval = monitoring_v3.TimeInterval(\n        start_time=start_time,\n        end_time=end_time\n    )\n\n    aggregation = monitoring_v3.Aggregation(\n        alignment_period={\"seconds\": 60 * minutes},\n        per_series_aligner=monitoring_v3.Aggregation.Aligner.ALIGN_MEAN,\n        cross_series_reducer=monitoring_v3.Aggregation.Reducer.REDUCE_MEAN,\n        group_by_fields=[\"metric.labels.instance_name\"]\n    )\n\n    results = client.list_time_series(\n        name=project_name,\n        filter=f'metric.type = \"{metric_type}\"',\n        interval=interval,\n        view=monitoring_v3.ListTimeSeriesRequest.TimeSeriesView.FULL,\n        aggregation=aggregation,\n    )\n\n    for series in results:\n        print(f\"Metric: {series.metric.type}\")\n        print(f\"Resource Labels: {series.resource.labels}\")\n        for point in series.points:\n            print(f\"  Point: {point.value.double_value} (Timestamp: {point.interval.end_time.isoformat()})\")\n",
            "filePath": "aggregate_metric_stats.py"
          },
